<title>USA: CBS buys broadcast rights to Clark book.</title>
<headline>CBS buys broadcast rights to Clark book.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>CBS Inc said Monday it acquired the broadcast rights to &quot;Without a Doubt,&quot; the memoir by Marcia Clark, the lead Los Angeles County prosecutor in the O.J. Simpson criminal trial.</p>
<p>Terms of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>CBS said the book will be the basis of a two-hour made-for-TV movie to be broadcast on the network.</p>
<p>CBS said Randy Robinson, who produced &quot;Amelia Earhart: The Final Flight&quot; for Time Warner Inc's TNT cable network, will be executive producer of the Clark movie.</p>
<p>CBS is a unit of Westinghouse Electric Corp.</p>
<p>((-- Jeff Benkoe, 212-859-1735.))</p>
